  "findings": [
    "An extra host copy can permit validated speculative preparation before the requested transfer; compare dependency and resource service time, not bytes alone.",
    "Paper targets confidential CPU–GPU I/O with FlexGen/PEFT weight swapping and historical vLLM parallel-sampling KV swapping. These are different data lifetimes.",
    "Measured single H100-SXM and VM do not include CPU TDX because the host lacks support; design assumptions and experimental protection scope differ.",
    "Read-only validation, nonce order and permitted batch reordering are correctness conditions; the artifact’s selected paths are not a full security validation.",
    "The zero-success-rate sequence ablation retains useful prepared ciphertext through reordering/NOP. It does not show that unused speculative work is free.",
    "Abstract/introduction/evaluation metrics remain ambiguous for 52.8%; Figure 6 final-step caption names data1 while its diagram shows data3. Originals retained and numerical claims not adopted."
